==English==
{{wp|+ (music)}}
[[Image:Drum sticks (cane rutes).jpg|thumb|Two styles of cane '''rutes'''|277x277px]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|ruthe}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Rute|gloss=rod, switch (slender woody plant stem)}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ro͞ot}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹuːt/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹʉwt/|a=SSB}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːt|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|root|route|qq2=some pronunciations}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|musical instruments}} A [[beater]] for [[drum]]s, consisting of a [[bundle]] of thin [[stick]]s, typically made of [[wood]], sometimes bound in such a way that the binding can be moved so that it varies the [[tightness]] of the binding.

====Usage notes====
Some consider rutes to be a sub-type of brushes and not distinct.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|switch}}
* {{l|en|dowel}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|brush}}

